           ('algebra', 'Cp = {{frac:(0.8)(2.772 hr⁻¹)(1000 mg)|(24 L)(2.772 − 0.0693) hr⁻¹}} (e^(−0.0693t) − e^(−2.772t))', 'The single oral dose equation is Cp = {{frac:F ka D0|VD(ka − k)}} (e^(−kt) − e^(−ka t)); F = 0.8 is the fraction absorbed, D0 = 1000 mg, VD = 24 L. On top, (0.8)(2.772)(1000) = 2217.6 mg·hr⁻¹; below, (24)(2.7027) = 64.86 L·hr⁻¹; the reciprocal hours cancel, so the coefficient is in mg/L.'),
