           ('algebra', 'Trough fraction at τ = 8 hr: {{frac:Cmin∞|Cmax∞}} = e^(−(0.231)(8)) = e^(−1.848) = 0.1576; a trough of 2 mg/L would need a peak of {{frac:2 mg/L|0.1576}} = 12.69 mg/L, above 10', 'With the interval fixed, the trough is always 0.1576 of the peak, whatever the dose, so raising the dose to lift the trough to 2 mg/L lifts the peak to 12.69 mg/L, outside the window. The dose cannot fix this; the interval has to change.'),
